.SH AUTH ON ACTION HOOKS
An auth on action policy can ask for a login again before these actions.
See
.B Auth On Action Policy
in
.BR otpme\-policy (1).
A dictionary has the hooks every object type has, and these; a command of another name is in brackets:
.RS
.PP
.na
.nh
add_words\ (word_import), dump.
.hy
.ad
.RE
.\" END AUTH ON ACTION HOOKS
.SH FILES
.na
.nh
.TP
\fI/var/lib/otpme/tree/\fR
The objects of the realm, on the nodes and, by sync, on the hosts.
A dictionary is the directory \fI<name>.dictionary\fR in the directory of its unit, e.g. \fI<realm>.realm/<site>.site/dictionaries.unit/german.dictionary/\fR.
Its entries are in \fIobject.json\fR, with the rest of its settings.
Change them with the commands above, not in the file.
.TP
\fI/etc/otpme/dicts/<name>.gz\fR
The words of the dictionaries a site comes with.
A file is read once, when the site adds its dictionary; changing the file later does not change the dictionary.
.hy
.ad
